# Elegy Acolyte's Void asks for a NONLAND permanent leaving the battlefield. On turn 3 Bot1 plays Strip Mine and uses it,
# sacrificing it (a land leaves) to destroy Bot2's Island (another land leaves): two permanents have left the battlefield,
# both lands, so no Robot token is created at the end step. The positive control, a nonland permanent of the opponent's
# leaving, is elegy-acolyte-void-an-opponents-permanent-bolted-makes-a-robot.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dark Ritual
Mox Ruby
Elegy Acolyte
Strip Mine
Island x2
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elegy Acolyte.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Island; Ability: Destroy)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Elegy Acolyte
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Strip Mine; Dark Ritual
